EC2: Elastic cloud compute.

	It is an Infrastructure as a service.
	It mainly consist of the capabilities of:
		Renting virtual machines(EC2)
		Storing data on virtual drives(EBS)
		Distributing loads across machines(ELB)
		Scaling the services using an auto-scaling group(ASG)

	
	EC2 sizing and Configuration options:

	a. Operating system: Linux, Windows or Mac OS
	b. How much compute power and cores(CPU)
	c. How much RAM
	d. How much storage space:
		Network-attached(EBS & EFS)
		hardware(EC2 Instance store)
	e. Network card: speed of the card, public IP address.
	f. Firewall rules: security group
	g. Bootstrap script(configure at first launch): EC2 User Data

		
	This EC2 user data is used to bootstrap the system at the first start. Means launching commands automatically when the machine starts.

	
