		So basically we can connect to the aws server using this ami and this server has preinstalled aws cli.
		So aws commands works on it like: aws iam list-users
		This throws an error and says: Unable to locate credentials. You can configure credentials by running "aws login".
		But never insert your aws api secret key and creds on an ec2 instance. As other can access this from the instance.
		So we have a solution. IAM Roles we had created before which an Instance uses to access the aws services on our behalf.

		So we are going to attach this role to our EC2 instance to provide it with the credentials.
		We can see that in the security section of the instance we donot have an IAM role attached to the instance.

		So for this we have to go to the Actions on the instance details page: Action -> Security -> Modify IAM role -> Choose the Role and 			Save/Update IAM role.
	
		
